  <h1>Combi vs System Boiler — Which Do I Need?</h1>
  <p>This is one of the first questions we get asked on almost every new boiler enquiry. There's no single right answer — it depends on your home, not just what's cheapest or newest. Here's how we actually think about it.</p>

  <h2>Combi boilers</h2>
  <p>A combi (combination) boiler heats water directly from the mains, on demand — no hot water cylinder, no cold water tank in the loft. Good for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Smaller to medium homes with one or two bathrooms</li>
    <li>Flats or homes with limited loft/airing cupboard space</li>
    <li>Households that don't run multiple hot taps or showers at exactly the same time</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The trade-off: if two showers run at once, pressure and temperature can dip, since it's all coming from one unit in real time.</p>

  <h2>System boilers</h2>
  <p>A system boiler heats water and stores it in a hot water cylinder, but most of the components are built into the boiler itself (unlike an older-style regular boiler, which needs a separate feed tank too). Good for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Larger homes with multiple bathrooms</li>
    <li>Households that want strong, consistent pressure even with more than one tap running</li>
    <li>Homes with solar thermal or planning to add it later</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The trade-off: you need space for a cylinder, and once the stored hot water runs out, you wait for it to reheat.</p>

  <h2>So which one do you need?</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Your situation</th><th>Usually suits</th></tr>
    <tr><td>1-2 bed home, one bathroom</td><td>Combi</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3+ bed home, multiple bathrooms, want strong simultaneous pressure</td><td>System</td></tr>
    <tr><td>No loft space or already have a combi you're happy with</td><td>Combi (like-for-like swap)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Currently on an old system with a tank, converting fully</td><td>Depends on the pipework — we'll check on the visit</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>What we won't do</h2>
  <p>We won't push you toward the bigger, more expensive option if a straightforward combi genuinely suits your home better — and we won't undersize a system boiler just to win the quote. Book a free visit and we'll give you a straight answer based on your actual home, not a generic recommendation.</p>
